* dsPIC33CK256MP508-Family Pin Definitions -- 48-Pin TQFP / UQFN
* Source: Microchip DS70005349K "dsPIC33CK256MP508 Family Data
*         Sheet", Pin Diagrams section (48-Pin TQFP, UQFN) and
*         Table 6 (48-Pin TQFP, UQFN pinout).
*
* Primary device: dsPIC33CK256MP505 -- determines this file's name.
*
* Companion devices -- all 48-pin family members share this exact
* pinout. Two independent axes distinguish family members, neither
* of which changes a single pin:
*   (1) Flash/RAM size (32K/64K/128K/256K program Flash) -- differs
*       in memory only, standard practice throughout this project.
*   (2) CAN FD presence -- the datasheet's own 48-Pin TQFP/UQFN pin
*       diagram is explicitly captioned for BOTH "dsPIC33CKXXXMP505"
*       (with CAN FD) and "dsPIC33CKXXXMP205" (without) together.
*       CAN FD is routed entirely via Peripheral Pin Select (RPn) --
*       there is no dedicated CAN pin at this or any other pin count
*       in this family -- so its presence/absence never affects the
*       physical pinout, only which peripheral modules exist behind
*       the RPn remap fabric.
* Per datasheet Table 1/Table 2 listing order (with-CAN-FD table
* before without-CAN-FD table, each descending by memory size):
*   dsPIC33CK256MP505, dsPIC33CK128MP505, dsPIC33CK64MP505,
*   dsPIC33CK32MP505, dsPIC33CK256MP205, dsPIC33CK128MP205,
*   dsPIC33CK64MP205, dsPIC33CK32MP205
*
* Package scope -- 48-Pin TQFP and 48-Pin UQFN are combined into
* this single file; both share one pin diagram/table in the
* datasheet (Fig./Table 6), differing only in package mechanicals.
* Per this project's established principle, physical pin numbers are
* not part of the .qpindef format, so any numbering difference
* between the two packages (if any) does not block combining them.
* The UQFN variant additionally has an exposed thermal pad on the
* bottom that may be left floating or tied to VSS -- not a distinct
* signal, no separate record needed (already covered by the G
* record below).
*
* NOT included -- the 28-Pin (MP502/MP202), 36-Pin (MP503/MP203),
* 64-Pin (MP506/MP206), and 80-Pin (MP508/MP208) family members all
* have measurably different pin counts and I/O availability per the
* datasheet's own family comparison tables (e.g. ADC channel counts,
* PWM pair counts) and are NOT pin-compatible with this 48-pin
* group. Each would need its own companion file.
*
* Flagged for manual review (dual-function / non-obvious pins):
*   MCLR    -- dedicated active-low Reset input; the datasheet lists
*             no GPIO alternate function for this pin at all (unlike
*             PC6 on the ATmega328 family). Classified I.
*   AVDD    -- separate ANALOG supply pin, distinct from digital VDD.
*             Classified I per this project's established workaround
*             for AVCC/AVDD-style pins (matches ATmega32/328 AVCC
*             treatment).
*   AVSS    -- separate ANALOG ground pin, distinct from digital VSS.
*             Unlike the ATmega family (no separate analog ground
*             pin there), this device has a genuinely distinct AVSS
*             pin. Classified I (not folded into the G record) since
*             it is architecturally a separate net from digital VSS,
*             consistent with AVDD's treatment.
*   RB0     -- OSCI/CLKI oscillator input is one alternate function
*             among several (AN5, RP32) on an otherwise ordinary
*             remappable GPIO pin -- this is a modern PPS-based part,
*             not a classic AVR with dedicated XTAL pins. Classified
*             B (GPIO-capable) like every other port pin; external
*             oscillator mode is a configuration-bit choice, not a
*             pin-dedication.
*   RB1     -- OSCO/CLKO, same reasoning as RB0. Classified B.
*   RB10    -- TMS (JTAG). Datasheet note: pulled up during erase/
*             programming when JTAG is enabled -- a transient
*             programming-time behavior, not a change to the pin's
*             GPIO classification. Classified B.
*   RB11/RB12/RB7 -- TCK/TDI/TDO (JTAG), same reasoning as RB10.
*             Classified B.
*   RB3/RB4/RB5/RB6/RB8/RB9 -- PGDn/PGCn (ICSP programming/debug),
*             same reasoning -- ordinary remappable GPIO pins whose
*             programming-time behavior does not change their B
*             classification.
*
* All other pins (RAx/RBx/RCx/RDx not listed above) are ordinary
* remappable-peripheral GPIO pins (ADC inputs, op-amp I/O, PWM
* outputs, comparators, UART/SPI/I2C via RPn, etc.) -- classified B.

D dsPIC33CK256MP508 Family 48-Pin TQFP/UQFN 16-bit Digital Signal Controller
P dsPIC33CK256MP505 dsPIC33CK128MP505 dsPIC33CK64MP505 dsPIC33CK32MP505 dsPIC33CK256MP205 dsPIC33CK128MP205 dsPIC33CK64MP205 dsPIC33CK32MP205

